{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>והעל</b> Two times in the Masorah: this one and the other: והעל אותם הר ההר, as stated in Pesaḥim. What did Ḥananiah, Mishael, and Azariah see that they surrendered themselves to the fiery furnace? They drew a qal va-ḥomer for themselves from the frogs — for the frogs surrendered themselves to death for the sanctification of the Name, and afterward were delivered, as written: וימותו הצפרדעים מן הבתים מן החצרות ומן השדות — but not from the ovens. But Moses and Aaron, concerning whom it is stated: יען לא האמנתם בי להקדישני — and they did not draw a qal va-ḥomer from the frogs — died and did not merit to enter the Land."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:11.829376574Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}